.Dd $Mdocdate$
.Dt QUARK_QUEUE_FILE_ACCESS_NAME_RESET 3
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm quark_queue_file_access_name_reset
.Nd clear file access names and start a new report generation
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.In quark.h
.Ft int
.Fn quark_queue_file_access_name_reset "struct quark_queue *qq"
.Sh DESCRIPTION
Removes all file access names from a queue opened with
.Dv QQ_FILE_ACCESS
and starts a new generation for repeated-open suppression.
After a successful reset, add the replacement names with
.Xr quark_queue_file_access_name_add 3 .
A process can then report an access class again, including a class reported
before the reset for the same file and path.
.Pp
Reset and addition are separate operations.
Opens while the name set is empty are not reported.
An open already in progress, or an event already in the queue, can still
refer to the previous name set.
Reset does not remove queued events.
.Pp
As with other operations on a queue, the caller must serialize reset and
name addition, including calls from processes that inherit the queue.
An error can leave only some names removed.
The queue remains usable; retry reset before adding replacement names.
.Sh RETURN VALUES
Zero on success, -1 on error with
.Va errno
set.
.Sh ERRORS
.Bl -tag -width Er
.It Er EINVAL
The queue does not have
.Dv QQ_FILE_ACCESS
with the eBPF backend.
.It Er EOVERFLOW
The generation reached its maximum value.
The names remain unchanged.
.El
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr quark_queue_file_access_name_add 3 ,
.Xr quark_queue_get_event 3 ,
.Xr quark_queue_open 3 ,
.Xr quark 7
